   "source": [
    "### 6A. Q–K subspace alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "The three rank measures above only bound each tensor's headroom in isolation. The sharper question is whether Q and K are **aligned** — whether K's variance lives in the directions Q actually reads.\n",
    "\n",
    "For each `(layer, kv_head)`:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **GQA-pool the Q second moment** across the 4 query heads that share this KV head:\n",
    "   $M_q^{(\\ell,\\, g)} \\;=\\; \\tfrac{1}{|g|} \\sum_{h \\in g} \\mathbb{E}[q_h q_h^\\top]$.\n",
    "   This is the aggregate second moment of every query that dots against this key.\n",
    "2. Eigendecompose $M_q^{(\\ell,\\,g)} = V \\Lambda V^\\top$, columns of $V$ sorted by descending eigenvalue.\n",
    "3. Measure the fraction of $K$'s total variance that lies inside $Q$'s top-$r$ subspace:\n",
    "   $$\\mathrm{align}(r) \\;=\\; \\frac{\\mathrm{tr}\\!\\bigl(V_{:,1:r}^\\top \\,\\mathbb{E}[k k^\\top]\\, V_{:,1:r}\\bigr)}{\\mathrm{tr}\\bigl(\\mathbb{E}[k k^\\top]\\bigr)}.$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Random-subspace baseline.** If $Q$'s basis were drawn uniformly at random (Haar on the Grassmannian), the expected captured fraction would be $r / d_h$. The dashed $y = r/d$ line in the overlay below marks this no-alignment null hypothesis:\n",
    "\n",
    "- curves **above** the line → $Q$'s top directions over-capture $K$'s variance; geometry-aware quantization has headroom.\n",
    "- curves **on** the line → $Q$ and $K$ are uncorrelated in basis; no headroom for $Q$-aware geometry beyond the uniform treatment.\n",
    "- curves **below** the line → $Q$'s top directions actively avoid $K$'s variance; $Q$-aware geometry would *hurt*.\n",
    "\n",
    "We use the **uncentered second moment** (`pooled[name][2]`) rather than centered covariance, because the quantization distortion $\\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[(q^\\top k - q^\\top \\hat k)^2\\right] = \\|k - \\hat k\\|^2_{\\mathbb{E}[q q^\\top]}$ is a quadratic form in the *uncentered* Q-moment, not the centered one. This matches the Stage 1 oracle-study convention."
   ]
  },
